The final stage is done. `verification-repair.json` is written with status **pass**, and a read-only dry run of the release gate on this run returns **eligible, no blockers, overall 8.5**. Nothing was published and no other repo files were changed.

**It only just clears the gate.** The weighted score is 8.48, which the gate's rounding turns into 8.5, the minimum for release. Enneagram scores exactly at its 8.0 minimum. The Type 6 read is honest at medium confidence, but Type 9 doesn't clearly lose; the article itself calls the 2002 step-back "close to even." If you want more margin before publishing, the best way to get it is new evidence, not more editing.

**What I checked:**
